# The Future Direction of Advanced Level Economics.

**Authors:** Lines, David

## Abstract
Discussing advanced level economics in England's secondary schools, Lines examines (1) underlying educational theory; (2) instruction guided by norm-referenced external examinations; and (3) the historical progress of those examinations. Referring to developmental psychology, he questions whether students are ready for the concepts taught, and advocates re-examination of the entire advanced level economics structure. (GEA)

